    onDialogueEnd:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
  - dialogueID: '"evil_eye"'
    lines:
    - text: It feels smooth and cold to the touch. I always wondered why they call
        it an "evil eye" if it's supposed to protect you.
      speakerName: 
      speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
      voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
      displayTime: 0
      requirePlayerInput: 0
      onLineStart:
        m_PersistentCalls:
          m_Calls: []
      onLineEnd:
        m_PersistentCalls:
          m_Calls: []
    canBeInterrupted: 0
    lockPlayerMovement: 0
    showSpeakerName: 0
    showPortrait: 0
    nextDialogueID: 
    requiresItem: 0
    requiredItemID: 
    onDialogueStart:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
    onDialogueEnd:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
  - dialogueID: '"bust"'
    lines:
    - text: It looks like me. Minus a few years or so. Why did they make this?
      speakerName: 
      speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
      voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
      displayTime: 0
      requirePlayerInput: 0
      onLineStart:
        m_PersistentCalls:
          m_Calls: []
      onLineEnd:
        m_PersistentCalls:
          m_Calls: []
    canBeInterrupted: 0
    lockPlayerMovement: 0
    showSpeakerName: 0
    showPortrait: 0
    nextDialogueID: 
    requiresItem: 0
    requiredItemID: 
    onDialogueStart:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
    onDialogueEnd:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
  - dialogueID: '"key"'
    lines:
    - text: The floor boards here are squeaky and loose. I'm suprised my dad let
        them get this bad.
      speakerName: 
      speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
      voiceClip: {fileID: 0}
      displayTime: 0
      requirePlayerInput: 0
      onLineStart:
        m_PersistentCalls:
